{
  "$comment": [
    "Per-camera resolution data for the full-resolution classifier and",
    "the timelapse heuristic. Keyed by canonical EXIF make+model string",
    "(uppercase + single-spaced, matching core/src/camera_names.rs::normalise()).",
    "",
    "Each value is an object:",
    "  natives:    list of [w, h] native sensor / max-photo modes the",
    "              full-resolution classifier matches against to decide",
    "              the FULL badge. Multiple entries cover bodies with",
    "              distinct still and open-gate video native modes.",
    "  video_max:  [w, h] or null. The camera's maximum *in-camera* video",
    "              recording resolution. When set, a recorded clip whose",
    "              pixel count strictly exceeds this is assumed to be a",
    "              timelapse — its dimensions are physically unreachable",
    "              for the camera's video pipeline, so it must have been",
    "              assembled from stills. Leave null for cameras whose",
    "              video and photo native match (cinema bodies, open-gate",
    "              MFT cams) — the heuristic stays silent rather than",
    "              risk false positives.",
    "",
    "Cameras shooting in a standard video format (3840x2160 UHD, 1920x1080",
    "FHD, etc.) match the deny-list in core/src/full_resolution.rs and",
    "land in the 'unknown' bucket for the full-resolution badge, regardless",
    "of what's in this file.",
    "",
    "Regenerate via: tools/fetch_sensor_resolutions.py",
    "Hand-edits inside the 'cameras' map are preserved by --fetch (Wikidata",
    "merge is additive). Both shape and the `natives` / `video_max` fields",
    "are validated on every run."
  ],
